## asymptote_mini.bot — fixture for `iterion bench asymptote`.
##
## The minimal shape the benchmark reads: a judge inside a bounded refine
## loop, so each pass through `review` leaves one verdict on the event stream
## at a known iteration index. The benchmark reconstructs the quality curve
## from those events alone — it never re-runs anything — so a stub-driven run
## produces exactly the data an operator's real run would.

schema draft:
  content: string

schema verdict:
  approved: bool
  notes: string

agent work:
  model: "claude-opus-4-7"
  output: draft

judge review:
  model: "claude-opus-4-7"
  output: verdict

workflow asymptote_mini:
  worktree: none
  sandbox: none
  entry: work

  budget:
    max_iterations: 20

  work -> review
  review -> done when approved
  review -> work as refine(5)
